r status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRANO, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOJIRI, KATSUHISA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KONDO, HISAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGAWA, HIDENORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUDA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGIYAMA, EIJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Compounds represented by general formula (I); and pharmaceutically acceptable salts or esters thereof, (wherein Y&lt;1&gt; is oxygen, NH, O-CO, O-SO2, O-CO-NH, O-CS-NH, NH-CO, NH-SO2, NH-CO-NH or NH-CS-NH; and R&lt;1&gt; is alkyl, alkenyl, alkynyl, aryl, aralkyl, arylalkenyl, arylalkynyl, cycloalkyl, cycloalkylalkyl, alkylcarbonyl, alkoxycarbonyl, arylcarbonyl or a heterocyclic group, provided these groups may be optionally substituted). The above compounds, salts and esters exert excellent antifungal effects on fungi against which the existing antifungal agents are not sufficiently efficacious, thus being useful as antifungal agents.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des composés représentés par la formule générale (I), ainsi que des sels ou esters de ceux-ci, acceptables sur le plan pharmacologique. Dans cette formule, Y&lt;1&gt; représente oxygène, NH, O-CO, O-SO2, O-CO-NH, O-CS-NH, NH-CO, NH-SO2, NH-CO-NH ou NH-CS-NH, et R&lt;1&gt; représente alkyle, alcényle, alcynyle, aryle, aralkyle, arylalcényle, arylalcynyle, cycloalkyle, cycloalkylalkyle, alkylcarbonyle, alcoxycarbonyle, arylcarbonyle ou un groupe hétérocyclique, à condition que ces groupes puissent être éventuellement substitués. Les composés ci-dessus, et leurs sels et esters, exercent d'excellents effets antifongiques sur des champignons contre lesquels les agents antifongiques existants ne sont pas suffisamment efficaces, et ils constituent donc des agents antifongiques utiles.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>